                         "id":  "INC-PCTM27-68291",
                         "isRepetitive":  false,
                         "machineNo":  "PCTM-27",
                         "natureOfFailure":  "Contacted Deutz Service Engineer, fixed the leakage with MSeal for temporary solution. Required the metal fuel pipe with part no. 0165-21-14. On 12.09.2026, The material has been dispatched from SCD by Bombax Logistics Pvt Ltd via air to Bangalore. Material expected to reach GDG-22.00 hrs.The material injector metallic pipe arrived at the machine at 22:30 hrs. Deutz Service Engineer attended the machine, and after the replacement of the metallic pipe, the machine was ready at 23:40 hrs.",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"On 09.09.2026, diesel leakage was observed from the metallic fuel pipe connecting the fuel pump and B3 cylinder fuel injector while PCTM-27 was moving from the siding at GDG for shunting. During the previous IOH at STMRD/UBL, the Deutz Service Engineer had carried out an engine health check, and no abnormality or leakage was observed in the fuel line.  The failure is therefore suspected to have developed subsequently, possibly due to vibration-induced fatigue of the metallic fuel pipe during engine operation. The OEM metallic fuel pipe (Part No. 0165-21-14) was procured from the authorized Deutz dealer, M/s South Kolkata Diesels, and replaced. The machine was made ready after replacement on 12.09.2026.  As a preventive measure, instructions have been issued to all machines fitted with similar Deutz engines, including CRCC-MPTs and PCTM-26, to periodically check the condition of the metallic fuel pipes, connections and clamps for cracks, vibration, looseness and leakage, and to take necessary corrective action.\"",
                         "repeatCount":  1,
