                         "dateOfRectification":  "2026-10-10",
                         "defectFamily":  "Air Compressor \u0026 Pneumatic Braking Defect",
                         "description":  "\"After completion of block,during the movement from BLLT (Left BLLT:- 16.05 hrs) to HAS at 16:50 hrs When waiting for Home Signal @ HAS at 16:50 Hrs Suddenly \"\"Brake Pressure (BP)\"\" dropped to Zero Pressure\"\" \u0026 \"\"Brake Cylinder Pressure\"\" raised to 3 Bar Pressure. So, Machine failed to move even after checking the Pneumatic system, All valves including C2W Relay Valve.\n \"",
                         "division":  "MYS",
                         "downHours":  0,
                         "fitTime":  "2026-10-10",
                         "id":  "INC-UTV004-79295",
                         "isRepetitive":  true,
                         "machineNo":  "UTV-004",
                         "natureOfFailure":  "\"After completion of block,during the movement from BLLT (Left BLLT:- 16.05 hrs) to HAS at 16:50 hrs When waiting for Home Signal @ HAS at 16:50 Hrs Suddenly \"\"Brake Pressure (BP)\"\" dropped to Zero Pressure\"\" \u0026 \"\"Brake Cylinder Pressure\"\" raised to 3 Bar Pressure. So, Machine failed to move even after checking the Pneumatic system, All valves including C2W Relay Valve.\n \"",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"On 09.09.2026, during movement from BLLT to HAS, the BP dropped to zero and the Brake Cylinder Pressure increased to 3 bar, resulting in failure of UTV-004 to move. On inspection, the failure was attributed to malfunction of the double check valve and magnetic valve in the emergency brake circuit. The machine was subsequently coupled with DUOMATIC-3324 and the section was cleared.  As a preventive and emergency measure, an emergency section-clearing procedure/flow chart was prepared for SAN Make UTV machines. In case of malfunction of the emergency brake circuit, the 30.6 stock cock can be closed to isolate the A9 brake line, enabling emergency clearing of the machine using the SA9 brake. The procedure was explained and discussed during the VC conducted on 15.09.2026.\"",
                         "repeatCount":  2,
