                         "defectFamily":  "Engine Radiator, Water Pump \u0026 Fan Defect",
                         "description":  "During the movement from KAG (Left KAG:- 11:05 hrs) to SLU at 11:25 hrs abnormal sound occurred. Then immediately stopped the M/C and checked the Engine. And found idler pulley\u0027s bearing of radiator fan belt has broken. Cleared the section at MYK at 11:29 hrs.",
                         "division":  "UBL",
                         "downHours":  24,
                         "fitTime":  "2026-09-09",
                         "id":  "INC-BRM56669-65736",
                         "isRepetitive":  true,
                         "machineNo":  "BRM-56669",
                         "natureOfFailure":  "During the movement from KAG (Left KAG:- 11:05 hrs) to SLU at 11:25 hrs abnormal sound occurred. Then immediately stopped the M/C and checked the Engine. And found idler pulley\u0027s bearing of radiator fan belt has broken. Cleared the section at MYK at 11:29 hrs.",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "The radiator fan idler pulley bearing of BRM-56669 was found damaged on 09.09.2026 during movement from KAG to SLU, resulting in abnormal sound. The bearing was replaced on the same day with a locally procured bearing. As per RDSO TM-203 (March 2017), the condition of the radiator fan drive bearing and shaft was checked during IOH at ZBD/YPR on 16.03.2026 and found satisfactory. The subsequent failure is assessed as bearing fatigue failure during service. As a preventive measure, the bearing and shaft shall be checked periodically for wear, excessive play, abnormal noise and other signs of deterioration, and necessary action shall be taken. A spare FAG 3307-BD-XL-2HRS-01 bearing was also issued from ZBD/YPR on 16.09.2026",
                         "repeatCount":  3,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "Recurring Engine Radiator, Water Pump \u0026 Fan Defect on BRM-56669 (3x cases)",
