                         "machineNo":  "MPT-12015",
                         "natureOfFailure":  "\"During working, the single-shaft assembly joint of the RH outer tamping bank at the front end, between the vibration unit and squeezing cylinder, was found broken. \nBlock Time\n23.05-00.06",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"The vibration shaft sub-assembly of MPT-12015 was found broken during operation. This is the first such failure reported in the HSPL (CRCC) MPT machine tamping bank. However, a similar issue of excessive play in the vibration shaft assembly was previously observed in MPT-12007.  In MPT-12007, excessive play was observed in the vertical 35 mm pin on 27.07.2026. Based on the recommendation of the HSPL Service Engineer, the vibration shaft sub-assembly was replaced on 31.07.2026.  The recurring issue was discussed with the OEM/CRCC during the Video Conference held on 02.09.2026, and the OEM was requested to furnish a detailed Root Cause Analysis (RCA) and corrective measures. The RCA was submitted by the OEM on 24.09.2026.  As per the OEM\u0027s RCA, the following corrective measures were recommended:  Reduction of the deceleration time of the tamping cycle to improve the hydraulic braking pressure of both the main vehicle and material vehicle, thereby reducing the impact/load transmitted to the tamping bank components. Design modification of the double-shaft connector and 35 mm pin to improve the strength and service reliability of the assembly. Timely replacement of the PG bush whenever excessive wear is observed, to prevent abnormal play and subsequent loading on the vibration shaft assembly.\"",
                         "repeatCount":  5,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "Recurring Tamping Vibration Shaft / Bearing Failure on MPT-12015 (5x cases)",
                         "slNo":  "2",
                         "sparesUsed":  "The work was stopped immediately and checked the outer tamping bank for any other damages. After observation, ramp out was given after locking RH outer tamping bank \u0026 cleared the section at 00.06 hrs. The machine can be made ready for working only after receipt and replacement of the required material. The material for the vibration shaft sub-assembly has been requested from HSPL. On 04.09.2026, Waiting for material. The HSPL service engineer, Mr. Sushil, is available with the machine. According to the Service Manager, Manish, the vibration shaft assembly has been dispatched from the HSPL warehouse in New Delhi. They will send the assembly by air to Bangalore through courier service. On 05.09.2026, Waiting for material. The material has been dispatched from New Delhi by air and is expected to be received on 06.09.2026 at ZBD/YPR. On 06.09.2026, Waiting for material, it has not yet been received at ZBD/YPR. Complete dismantling of the RH Outer Tamping Bank vibration shaft has been completed. On 07.09.2026, The required material was received at ZBD/YPR at 13:00 hrs. Thereafter, the material was dispatched to KIGL by 2-ton vehicle and received at site at 15:30 hrs. Assembly work commenced at 16:00 hrs. On 08.09.2026, the complete RH Outer Tamping Bank vibration shaft assembly was assembled and checked. The machine was tested(01:10hrs) and found to be working satisfactorily. M/c made ready for working.",
