                         "defectFamily":  "",
                         "description":  "Category: Pneumatic\nBlock section: SSPN-BSPL\nBlock time: 14.20-15.20 hrs\nDuring clearing of block, at 15.15 hrs, driving mode not engaging. checking the issue at site, manually engaged the gear box \u0026 clear the section SSPN @ 15.50",
                         "division":  "SBC",
                         "downHours":  0,
                         "fitTime":  "2026-10-25",
                         "id":  "INC-BRM027-29842",
                         "isRepetitive":  false,
                         "machineNo":  "BRM-027",
                         "natureOfFailure":  "Category: Pneumatic\nBlock section: SSPN-BSPL\nBlock time: 14.20-15.20 hrs\nDuring clearing of block, at 15.15 hrs, driving mode not engaging. checking the issue at site, manually engaged the gear box \u0026 clear the section SSPN @ 15.50",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"TOn 25.10.2026, during block clearance in the SSPNÃ¢â‚¬â€œBSPL section, the machine\u0027s driving mode failed to engage. On inspection, the pneumatic valve No. 90344, which controls the gearbox engaging/disengaging pneumatic cylinder, was found malfunctioning due to moisture ingress.  The moisture ingress was attributed to the failure of the relay in EL-T 1163 PCB, which supplies 24V power to the pneumatic air dryer. Due to the relay failure, the air dryer could not function properly, resulting in moisture accumulation in the pneumatic system and subsequent malfunction of the pneumatic valve.  During further inspection by the deputed Plasser Service Engineer, axle No. 2 was opened and damage was noticed on the engaging face of the pinion gear assembly (Part No. SSP70.01.602AE). The damaged assembly was also considered a possible contributing factor to the driving-mode engagement problem. Preventive action. The machine\u0027s grounding connections were also instructed to be checked and cleaned. Ensure proper functioning of the pneumatic air dryer and periodically check the 24V power supply and relay circuit of the EL-T 1163 PCB.\"",
                         "repeatCount":  1,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "",
                         "slNo":  "10",
                         "sparesUsed":  "\"Replaced the pneumatic valve -90344 which controls the drive engaging \u0026 dis engaging pneumatic cylinder, \u0026 Cleared the scetion at SSPN at 15.50hrs\nThe defective pneumatic valve No. 90344 was replaced.\n\nThe EL-T 1163 PCB was temporarily bypassed to restore operation. Similar PCBs had already been sent to Plasser India for repair.\nAxle No. 2 was opened and the damaged pinion gear assembly (Part No. SSP70.01.602AE) was replaced on 27.10.2026.\n\nThe machine\u0027s grounding connections were also instructed to be checked and cleaned\"",
                         "status":  "FIT",
                         "stepsTaken":  "\"Replaced the pneumatic valve -90344 which controls the drive engaging \u0026 dis engaging pneumatic cylinder, \u0026 Cleared the scetion at SSPN at 15.50hrs\nThe defective pneumatic valve No. 90344 was replaced.\n\nThe EL-T 1163 PCB was temporarily bypassed to restore operation. Similar PCBs had already been sent to Plasser India for repair.\nAxle No. 2 was opened and the damaged pinion gear assembly (Part No. SSP70.01.602AE) was replaced on 27.10.2026.\n\nThe machine\u0027s grounding connections were also instructed to be checked and cleaned\"",
