                         "natureOfFailure":  "Date of failure:25.10.2026\nBlock Section-BSN-RDI\nBlock Time - 03:00-05:00 hrs, cleared at 05:15 hrs\nAfter 100 mtrs packing in 2 nd location between BSN-RDI,LH outer Tamping up/dn cylinder cut from frame.Mc closed@04:50 hrs.After pway manual packing, Mc  cleared RDI at 05:15 hrs.",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"During tamping operations on 25.10.2026 in BSNÃ¢â‚¬â€œRDI section, after completing approximately 100 metres of packing at the second location, the LH outer tamping unit up/down cylinder holding frame broke, resulting in detachment of the cylinder from the frame. The machine was closed at 04:50 hrs, and after manual packing by P-Way staff, the section was cleared at 05:15 hrs.  The failure is suspected to have occurred due to repeated impact and dynamic loads transmitted to the up/down cylinder holding frame during tamping operations. Continuous cyclic loading may have resulted in fatigue and eventual fracture of the frame.  A similar failure was reported in MPT-56577 on 19.10.2026, wherein the RH tamping unit up/down cylinder outer holding bracket broke due to suspected impact loading during tamping operations. The recurrence of similar failures in the cylinder holding frames indicates the need to examine their structural strength and design adequacy under repeated operational impact loads.  As an immediate corrective measure, the broken LH outer tamping unit up/down cylinder holding frame was welded, and the issue was rectified.             Convert to PDF       add the action taken also the MPT56943 part is welded by e6013 electrode on next day \u0026 trail taken at siding found satisfactory, prefer E7016 Electrode is suggesting for strength welding for the impact load location ,also add the in 100 hours schedule chek any crack at the frame of the up/dn cylinder gholding bracket during schedule maintenance to avoid the failre in block section add these points too              Failure Analysis Ã¢â‚¬â€œ LH Outer Tamping Unit Up/Down Cylinder Holding Frame During tamping operations on 25.10.2026 in BSNÃ¢â‚¬â€œRDI section, after completing approximately 100 metres of packing at the second location, the LH outer tamping unit up/down cylinder holding frame broke, resulting in detachment of the cylinder from the frame. The machine was closed at 04:50 hrs, and after manual packing by P-Way staff, the section was cleared at 05:15 hrs.  The failure is suspected to have occurred due to repeated impact and dynamic loads transmitted to the up/down cylinder holding frame during tamping operations. Continuous cyclic loading may have resulted in fatigue and eventual fracture of the frame.  A similar failure was reported in MPT-56577 on 19.10.2026, wherein the RH tamping unit up/down cylinder outer holding bracket broke due to suspected impact loading during tamping operations. The recurrence of similar failures indicates the need to examine the structural strength and design adequacy of the cylinder holding frames under repeated operational impact loads.  Action Taken:  The broken LH outer tamping unit up/down cylinder holding frame was welded using an E6013 electrode on the following day. Subsequently, a trial was conducted in the siding, and the working was found satisfactory.  Preventive Measures: 1. For welding repairs at locations subjected to repeated impact and dynamic loading, the use of E7016 low-hydrogen electrodes is recommended to achieve higher weld strength and better resistance to cracking, subject to the approved welding procedure and material compatibility. 2. The OEM should examine the recurring failures in MPT-56577 and MPT-56943 and assess the structural strength of the up/down cylinder holding brackets. Suitable design strengthening or modification should be considered. 3. During every 100-hour schedule maintenance, the up/down cylinder holding brackets and frames shall be thoroughly inspected for cracks, deformation and signs of fatigue. 4. Any initial cracks or structural defects identified during scheduled maintenance should be rectified immediately to prevent bracket failure during block working\"",
                         "repeatCount":  1,
