                         "natureOfFailure":  "Block section \u0026 time: BWT - MKM; 00:15 to 03:00 hrs\n Failure time: 02:10 hrs \n Block cleared time:02:57 hrs at BWT\n Category:Mechanical \n Description of failure: During working Engine suddenly shutdown. Found engine radiator fan not rotating. \n Action taken: Failure Reason: During the line block between BWT and MKM Single line, the line block was from 00:15 to 03:00 hrs. \nDuring working at 02:10 hrs, the engine shut down, and upon inspection, it was found that the radiator fan was not rotating. The engine was restarted after adding water to the radiator fins. \nThe machine was then  locked and the section was cleared at BWT road 4 at 02:57 hrs.",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"During working in BWTÃ¢â‚¬â€œMKM Single Line section on 24.10.2026, the engine suddenly shut down at 02:10 hrs due to non-functioning of the radiator fan. On inspection at the siding, it was found that the double cooling pump was not delivering oil, resulting in non-operation of the radiator fan, ZF cooler fan and hydraulic cooler fans.  On dismantling the cooling pump, the pump shaft, coupler and bearings were found worn out. The shaft failure is suspected to have occurred due to fatigue resulting from prolonged service and continuous operational loading, as the shaft had not been replaced earlier.  The existing shaft (Part No. WN81.303), having a length of 215 mm, 14 internal splines and 16 external splines, is designed for the double pump arrangement. The corresponding shaft specifications must be maintained while replacing the shaft, as WN81.503 is intended for variable pump applications and WN81.703, though of the same length, has 16 internal splines and is intended for triple pump applications. Hence, correct shaft selection is essential to ensure proper fitment and reliable power transmission.  The damaged bearings, shaft and associated components were attended to, and the cooling pump was reassembled. After replacement and fitment on 27.10.2026, the machine was tested, and the radiator fan, ZF cooler fan and hydraulic cooler fans were found working satisfactorily.  Preventive Measure: The condition of the cooling pump shaft, coupler and bearings should be checked during scheduled maintenance. Replacement of the shaft and associated components should be considered based on their condition to prevent fatigue-related failures and sudden engine shutdowns\"",
                         "repeatCount":  2,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "Recurring Engine Radiator, Water Pump \u0026 Fan Defect on CSM-939 (2x cases)",
                         "slNo":  "38",
                         "sparesUsed":  "Action taken: At siding, checked Cooling pump (Double pump) outputs and found no discharge of oil and found that ZF cooler fan, Hydraulic cooler fans also not rotating. Requires Cooling pump(Part No: HY806X.20.14LI and ZF mounting accessories. Opened the Cooling pump and found that pump shaft, coupler and bearing all got worn out. Bearings has been arranged from coimbatore \u0026 is expected to reach on Monday(26.10.2026) \u0026 shaft is not available in ZBD/YPR \u0026 has been arranged from RYP which will be dispacted on Monday(26.10.2026). On 25.10.2026, Waiting for materials. On 26.10.2026, the bearing from Coimbatore arrived at 16:00 hrs. On 27.10.2026, Bearing fixed to the carrier at ZBD/YPR and reached machine at 12:50 hrs. Carrier housing removed from ZF Gear box. Assembled the carrier on the housing. Fixed the housing to ZF. Fixed the cooling pump. Machine tested; all cooling fans and radiator fan working properly. Systems found satisfactory, and the machine is ready at 17.45 hrs for the night block.",
                         "status":  "FIT",
                         "stepsTaken":  "Action taken: At siding, checked Cooling pump (Double pump) outputs and found no discharge of oil and found that ZF cooler fan, Hydraulic cooler fans also not rotating. Requires Cooling pump(Part No: HY806X.20.14LI and ZF mounting accessories. Opened the Cooling pump and found that pump shaft, coupler and bearing all got worn out. Bearings has been arranged from coimbatore \u0026 is expected to reach on Monday(26.10.2026) \u0026 shaft is not available in ZBD/YPR \u0026 has been arranged from RYP which will be dispacted on Monday(26.10.2026). On 25.10.2026, Waiting for materials. On 26.10.2026, the bearing from Coimbatore arrived at 16:00 hrs. On 27.10.2026, Bearing fixed to the carrier at ZBD/YPR and reached machine at 12:50 hrs. Carrier housing removed from ZF Gear box. Assembled the carrier on the housing. Fixed the housing to ZF. Fixed the cooling pump. Machine tested; all cooling fans and radiator fan working properly. Systems found satisfactory, and the machine is ready at 17.45 hrs for the night block.",
