                         "machineNo":  "BRM-56680",
                         "natureOfFailure":  "Description of failure: During maintenance, the lube oil pressure sensor malfunctioned, causing frequent engine shutdowns.",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"During operation at GDG siding on 24.10.2026, fluctuations in the engine lubricating oil pressure were observed. The machine is fitted with a Deutz BF 8M-1015CP engine. The 2nd IOH was completed on 02.10.2026 at 4,965 EH, and the present engine reading is 5,042 EH, indicating only 77 EH of operation after the 2nd IOH.  The Deutz Service Engineer inspected the engine on 25.10.2026 and observed that the lubricating oil pressure was not being maintained at both idle and full RPM. Excessive crankshaft bearing clearance was suspected as the probable cause of the pressure fluctuation. Considering the inability to maintain the required lubricating oil pressure, the OEM recommended a major engine overhaul.  Since the issue was observed immediately after the 2nd IOH, the premature occurrence of the failure requires detailed investigation by the OEM to establish the root cause and assess the quality of the overhaul work and associated components.  The engine was dismantled and removed from the machine at STMRD/UBL on 30.10.2026 and transported to SCD Pune Workshop for detailed inspection and major overhaul. The engine reached SCD Pune on 31.10.2026, where unloading and further dismantling activities were initiated Further Action: A detailed inspection report and Root Cause Analysis (RCA) from Deutz/SCD Pune shall be obtained, particularly regarding crankshaft bearing clearance, lubrication system condition and the reason for the premature failure\"",
                         "repeatCount":  1,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "",
                         "slNo":  "5",
                         "sparesUsed":  "\"Failure reason: Fluctuations in the lubrication oil pressure were observed at GDG siding.\n\nEngine model: BF 8M-1015CP  \n2nd IOH attended: 02.10.2026 (EH-4965)  \nPresent EH:5042\n\nOn 25.10.2026, Deutz SE Mr. Babu attended the machine. According to the service engineerÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s report, there was an issue with the engine oil pressure at both idle and full RPM. The crankshaft bearing clearance issue was suspected, and the lubricating oil pressure was not being maintained. Therefore, a major engine overhaul was recommended.\n\nOn 26.10.2026, the matter was discussed with the OEM, who also recommended an overhaul.\n\nOn 27.10.2026, a request was placed with Deutz SE to dismantle the engine.\n\nThe machine was moved to UBL after being coupled with RBMV-007. \nleft GDG at 00:30, arrived at UBL at 02:05, \n stabled at FCI siding at 03:05.\n\nOn 28.10.2026,\nDismantling of the engine top cover and other accessories was planned. However, due to shunting movements in the UBL yard, movement of the machine from FCI siding to STMRD/UBL was not permitted.\n\nOn 29.10.2026 \nDeutz SE reported the machine at UBL at 09:00 hrs.\n\nThe machine arrived at STMRD 11:00 hrs.\nAll engine accessories are Dismantled up to 19.00 hrs\nOn 30.10.2026\nThe Engine lifted from the machine at 12.30 hrs.\nAfter Making the frame the Engine loaded into the transport vehicle (no.KA16-AA 4262)  at 15.00 hrs\nThe Vehicle left to SCD Pune Workshop at 16.30 hrs from STMRD\n\nOn 31.10.2026\nThe transport vehicle reached SCD Pune at 12:20 hrs.  \nUnloading the engine \u0026 kept inside the work shop \nDismantled the radiator from the engine.\"",
                         "status":  "FIT",
                         "stepsTaken":  "\"Failure reason: Fluctuations in the lubrication oil pressure were observed at GDG siding.\n\nEngine model: BF 8M-1015CP  \n2nd IOH attended: 02.10.2026 (EH-4965)  \nPresent EH:5042\n\nOn 25.10.2026, Deutz SE Mr. Babu attended the machine. According to the service engineerÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s report, there was an issue with the engine oil pressure at both idle and full RPM. The crankshaft bearing clearance issue was suspected, and the lubricating oil pressure was not being maintained. Therefore, a major engine overhaul was recommended.\n\nOn 26.10.2026, the matter was discussed with the OEM, who also recommended an overhaul.\n\nOn 27.10.2026, a request was placed with Deutz SE to dismantle the engine.\n\nThe machine was moved to UBL after being coupled with RBMV-007. \nleft GDG at 00:30, arrived at UBL at 02:05, \n stabled at FCI siding at 03:05.\n\nOn 28.10.2026,\nDismantling of the engine top cover and other accessories was planned. However, due to shunting movements in the UBL yard, movement of the machine from FCI siding to STMRD/UBL was not permitted.\n\nOn 29.10.2026 \nDeutz SE reported the machine at UBL at 09:00 hrs.\n\nThe machine arrived at STMRD 11:00 hrs.\nAll engine accessories are Dismantled up to 19.00 hrs\nOn 30.10.2026\nThe Engine lifted from the machine at 12.30 hrs.\nAfter Making the frame the Engine loaded into the transport vehicle (no.KA16-AA 4262)  at 15.00 hrs\nThe Vehicle left to SCD Pune Workshop at 16.30 hrs from STMRD\n\nOn 31.10.2026\nThe transport vehicle reached SCD Pune at 12:20 hrs.  \nUnloading the engine \u0026 kept inside the work shop \nDismantled the radiator from the engine.\"",
