                         "natureOfFailure":  "Category:electrical\n M/c under warranty.\n Description of failure: During maintenance RH side track lifting found to be not functioning due to Servo current leakage.",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"During maintenance on 23.10.2026, the RH-side track lifting unit of MPT-12015 was found not functioning due to malfunctioning of the servo valve, resulting in improper lifting operation and hunting. The hydraulic working brake was also reported to have stopped functioning during siding testing.  The machine was commissioned on 02.09.2025 and is still under warranty. Initially, the servo DC valve was checked and cleaned, and the height transducer was inspected; however, the problem could not be rectified. On further examination, the HSPL Service Engineer suspected malfunctioning of the RH-side Moog servo valve. The servo valve available with MPT-56591 was found to be of a different model and could not be fitted due to warranty restrictions and model compatibility requirements.  The correct CRCC servo valve (Part No. 40095887) was subsequently arranged by the OEM and received on 28.10.2026. After replacement of the servo valve by the HSPL Service Engineer, the RH lifting unit was tested in the siding and found working satisfactorily. The machine was made ready on 28.10.2026. OEM Review: Since the machine is under warranty, the OEM (HSPLÃ¢â‚¬â€œCRCC) shall be requested to investigate the premature failure of the servo valve, submit a detailed Root Cause Analysis (RCA) and recommend suitable preventive measures. The issue, along with the prolonged material arrangement and warranty-related repair constraints, is proposed to be reviewed during the OEM meeting planned for the second week of November 2026\"",
                         "repeatCount":  1,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "",
                         "slNo":  "2",
                         "sparesUsed":  "Action taken: Checked and cleaned Servo DC valve \u0026 checked Height transducer. Problem could not be identified. Further waiting for SE. On 24.10.2026, HSPL SE arrived to machine and repair is under process, RH side servo valve malfuntioning suspected. the servo valve of same brand is available with MPT 56591. On 25.10.2026, the servo valve received from MPT-56591 was found to be of a different model. Due to warranty restrictions, only the correct CRCC servo valve can be fitted. HSPL SE Shri Manish has arranged the demand for the correct valve. On 26.10.2026 the servo valve was dispatched from the Delhi warehouse by Train No. 22692 (KSR Rajdhani) and is expected to reach the machine on 28.10.2026. On 27.10.2026 the servo valve was dispatched and is expected to reach the machine on 28.10.2026. On 28.10.2026 servo valve replaced \u0026 m/c made ready",
