                         "natureOfFailure":  "Block section: KDN-BAY \nFailure Time.16.20\nBlock cleared time:16.30\nCategory: Electrical\nDecription of failure: During ramp out  of block, machine was experiencing electrical issue of auto brake release in working mode signal resulting in interrupted forward and backward movement of machine. Machine cleared block in time with no detention",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"During ramping out of the block on 22.10.2026 in KDNÃ¢â‚¬â€œBAY section, the machine experienced an intermittent electrical issue in the auto brake release signal in working mode, resulting in interrupted forward and backward movement.  On inspection, all work-drive mode input sensors and the pressure-switch supplies from the working and front cabin brake units were found satisfactory. Further investigation revealed a loose connection in the input wiring of pressure switch 1F6 at the B-94 panel, resulting in interruption of the signal supply to the working cabin B-7. The loose connection was rectified by tightening the input wire, and the machine\u0027s working was tested and found satisfactory. Preventive Action During POH, the tightness of all electrical panel wiring connections, particularly input signal terminals and pressure-switch connections, shall be thoroughly checked. Further, it is recommended to include checking and tightening of electrical panel wiring connections in the 100-hour schedule maintenance to prevent recurrence of similar failures due to loose electrical connection\"",
                         "repeatCount":  1,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "",
                         "slNo":  "5",
