                         "natureOfFailure":  "Block section: LHN - IDR U/L\n Block time: 13.00-14.00 hrs\n Failure time: 13.40 hrs\n Block cleared time: 14.05 Hrs\n Category:Mechanical \n Description of Failure: During the 2nd block, the RH TB up-and-down cylinde outer holding frame broken. The tamping units were lifted using a mechanical jack and all units securely locked and the block was cleared.",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"During the second block on 19.10.2026 in LHNÃ¢â‚¬â€œIDR U/L section, the outer holding bracket of the RH tamping unit up/down cylinder broke at approximately 13:40 hrs. The failure is suspected to have occurred due to repeated impact and dynamic loading transmitted to the up/down cylinder and its holding bracket during tamping operations. Continuous cyclic loading over the years may have resulted in fatigue and eventual fracture of the bracket.  The machine was commissioned in 2020 and has been in operation for approximately six years. As an immediate corrective measure, the broken bracket was welded using an E7018 electrode, which provides a high-tensile-strength weld joint, and the machine was restored to working condition. The machine\u0027s POH was planned on 30.10.2026 at CPOH/RYP, and the machine is presently under movement to RYP for POH attention. The damaged RH up/down cylinder outer holding bracket will be replaced during POH.\"",
                         "repeatCount":  1,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "",
                         "slNo":  "7",
                         "sparesUsed":  "\"Actions taken: The broken RH up/down cylinder outer holding bracket was repaired by arc welding using an E7018 low-hydrogen electrode. The electrode, having a tensile strength of approximately 70,000 psi, provides high ductility, impact resistance and a strong weld joint suitable for structural and load-bearing applications. Its low-hydrogen properties also help minimise the risk of hydrogen-induced cracking after welding.\n\nThe welding work was completed on the night of 20.10.2026. The test block was conducted on siding on 21.10.2026 found working satisfacory\"",
                         "status":  "FIT",
                         "stepsTaken":  "\"Actions taken: The broken RH up/down cylinder outer holding bracket was repaired by arc welding using an E7018 low-hydrogen electrode. The electrode, having a tensile strength of approximately 70,000 psi, provides high ductility, impact resistance and a strong weld joint suitable for structural and load-bearing applications. Its low-hydrogen properties also help minimise the risk of hydrogen-induced cracking after welding.\n\nThe welding work was completed on the night of 20.10.2026. The test block was conducted on siding on 21.10.2026 found working satisfacory\"",
                         "subsystem":  "Mechanical",
