                         "_features":  {
                                           "fullTxt":  "block section:blhi-dru s/l\n block time: 21:30-03:00 hrs\n block cleared time: 03.00hrs\n category:mechanical \n m/c under warranty.\n description of failure: during block after working 1600 meters, rh side tamping unit big squeezing cylinder piston head was broken. mechanical component block section:blhi-dru s/l\n block time: 21:30-03:00 hrs\n block cleared time: 03.00hrs\n category:mechanical \n m/c under warranty.\n description of failure: during block after working 1600 meters, rh side tamping unit big squeezing cylinder piston head was broken.  waiting hspl se \u0026 the material (oil gripping cylinder part code- 23067083) spoke to the hspl service manager, has deputed service engineer mr. sachin to attend the issue. on 14 \u002615.10.2026, waiting for material \u0026 se. on 16.10.2026, hspl se arrived to the m/c.checked the material received . on 17.10.2026 hspl service engineer attended all tool-tilting cylinders, 4 nos. of 65 mm pins, and 8 nos. of rh/lh outer tamping tool holders removed. lubrication sleeves of lh outer front and rear tool holders removed. on 18.10.2026 rh front and rear tool holder lubrication sleeves (04 nos.) and lh front/rear 65 mm pin lubrication sleeves (02 nos.) and rh front 65 mm pin lubrication sleeve (01 no.) removed. rh rear squeezing cylinder fitted. worn-out portions of all inner tamping tool holders welded. inner threads of lh front and rh rear tool-holding bolts reconditioned. m/c repair is under progress. on 19.10.2026, replaced 4 sets of 65 mm pins, sleeves, copper spacers, bushes \u0026 2 lh square cylinder assemblies. fitted 4 tool holder assemblies, 8 tamping tools and 8 tool-tilting cylinders. connected greasing hoses and completed greasing. m/c made ready at 18.00 hrs \u0026 trial block attended(18.10-19.00 hrs; shyp yd rd 3, 300 mtrs) - waiting hspl se \u0026 the material (oil gripping cylinder part code- 23067083) spoke to the hspl service manager, has deputed service engineer mr. sachin to attend the issue. on 14 \u002615.10.2026, waiting for material \u0026 se. on 16.10.2026, hspl se arrived to the m/c.checked the material received . on 17.10.2026 hspl service engineer attended all tool-tilting cylinders, 4 nos. of 65 mm pins, and 8 nos. of rh/lh outer tamping tool holders removed. lubrication sleeves of lh outer front and rear tool holders removed. on 18.10.2026 rh front and rear tool holder lubrication sleeves (04 nos.) and lh front/rear 65 mm pin lubrication sleeves (02 nos.) and rh front 65 mm pin lubrication sleeve (01 no.) removed. rh rear squeezing cylinder fitted. worn-out portions of all inner tamping tool holders welded. inner threads of lh front and rh rear tool-holding bolts reconditioned. m/c repair is under progress. on 19.10.2026, replaced 4 sets of 65 mm pins, sleeves, copper spacers, bushes \u0026 2 lh square cylinder assemblies. fitted 4 tool holder assemblies, 8 tamping tools and 8 tool-tilting cylinders. connected greasing hoses and completed greasing. m/c made ready at 18.00 hrs \u0026 trial block attended(18.10-19.00 hrs; shyp yd rd 3, 300 mtrs)",
                                           "primaryTxt":  "block section:blhi-dru s/l\n block time: 21:30-03:00 hrs\n block cleared time: 03.00hrs\n category:mechanical \n m/c under warranty.\n description of failure: during block after working 1600 meters, rh side tamping unit big squeezing cylinder piston head was broken. mechanical component block section:blhi-dru s/l\n block time: 21:30-03:00 hrs\n block cleared time: 03.00hrs\n category:mechanical \n m/c under warranty.\n description of failure: during block after working 1600 meters, rh side tamping unit big squeezing cylinder piston head was broken."
                                       },
                         "actionTaken":  "Waiting HSPL SE \u0026 the material (oil gripping cylinder part code- 23067083) Spoke to the HSPL service manager, has deputed Service Engineer Mr. Sachin to attend the issue. On 14 \u002615.10.2026, Waiting for material \u0026 SE. On 16.10.2026, HSPL SE arrived to the M/c.Checked the material received . On 17.10.2026 HSPL Service Engineer attended all tool-tilting cylinders, 4 nos. of 65 mm pins, and 8 nos. of RH/LH outer tamping tool holders removed. Lubrication sleeves of LH outer front and rear tool holders removed. On 18.10.2026 RH front and rear tool holder lubrication sleeves (04 nos.) and LH front/rear 65 mm pin lubrication sleeves (02 nos.) and RH front 65 mm pin lubrication sleeve (01 no.) removed. RH rear squeezing cylinder fitted. Worn-out portions of all inner tamping tool holders welded. Inner threads of LH front and RH rear tool-holding bolts reconditioned. M/c repair is under Progress. On 19.10.2026, Replaced 4 sets of 65 mm pins, sleeves, copper spacers, bushes \u0026 2 LH square cylinder assemblies. Fitted 4 tool holder assemblies, 8 tamping tools and 8 tool-tilting cylinders. Connected greasing hoses and completed greasing. M/c made ready at 18.00 hrs \u0026 trial block attended(18.10-19.00 hrs; SHYP Yd Rd 3, 300 mtrs)",
                         "breakdownTime":  "2026-10-12",
                         "category":  "MPT",
