                         "dateOfRectification":  "2026-10-19",
                         "defectFamily":  "",
                         "description":  "Block section:BLHI-DRU S/L\n Block time: 21:30-03:00 hrs\n Block cleared time: 03.00Hrs\n Category:Mechanical \n M/c under warranty.\n Description of Failure: During block after working 1600 meters, RH side Tamping unit Big squeezing cylinder piston head was broken.",
                         "division":  "MYS",
                         "downHours":  144,
                         "fitTime":  "2026-10-19",
                         "id":  "INC-MPT12007-18164",
                         "isRepetitive":  false,
                         "machineNo":  "MPT-12007",
                         "natureOfFailure":  "Block section:BLHI-DRU S/L\n Block time: 21:30-03:00 hrs\n Block cleared time: 03.00Hrs\n Category:Mechanical \n M/c under warranty.\n Description of Failure: During block after working 1600 meters, RH side Tamping unit Big squeezing cylinder piston head was broken.",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"During machine working on 12.10.2026 in BLHIÃ¢â‚¬â€œDRU Single Line section, after completion of approximately 1,600 metres of tamping, the piston head of the RH-side big squeezing cylinder broke, resulting in malfunctioning of the RH tamping unit. The failure may be attributed to excessive operational stress or fatigue of the piston head. However, the exact root cause requires detailed examination by the OEM (HSPL).  The machine was attended by the HSPL Service Engineer, and comprehensive repairs were carried out, including replacement of the RH rear squeezing cylinder, 65 mm pins, lubrication sleeves, bushes, copper spacers and two LH square cylinder assemblies. The machine was made ready on 19.10.2026 and successfully tested during a trial block of 300 metres.  Further, during the previous OEM meeting held on 02.09.2026 with HSPLÃ¢â‚¬â€œCRCC, the OEM had assured that the first trial of the newly designed vibration shaft assembly and 35 mm pin would be conducted on MPT-12007. However, the trial had not been conducted up to 31.10.2026. In view of the pending design improvements and recurring tamping unit-related issues, a review meeting with the OEM is proposed during the second week of November 2026 to obtain the status of the design modifications and discuss the failure, along with suitable corrective and preventive measures to avoid recurrence.\"",
                         "repeatCount":  1,
                         "repetitiveReason":  "",
                         "slNo":  "7",
                         "sparesUsed":  "Waiting HSPL SE \u0026 the material (oil gripping cylinder part code- 23067083) Spoke to the HSPL service manager, has deputed Service Engineer Mr. Sachin to attend the issue. On 14 \u002615.10.2026, Waiting for material \u0026 SE. On 16.10.2026, HSPL SE arrived to the M/c.Checked the material received . On 17.10.2026 HSPL Service Engineer attended all tool-tilting cylinders, 4 nos. of 65 mm pins, and 8 nos. of RH/LH outer tamping tool holders removed. Lubrication sleeves of LH outer front and rear tool holders removed. On 18.10.2026 RH front and rear tool holder lubrication sleeves (04 nos.) and LH front/rear 65 mm pin lubrication sleeves (02 nos.) and RH front 65 mm pin lubrication sleeve (01 no.) removed. RH rear squeezing cylinder fitted. Worn-out portions of all inner tamping tool holders welded. Inner threads of LH front and RH rear tool-holding bolts reconditioned. M/c repair is under Progress. On 19.10.2026, Replaced 4 sets of 65 mm pins, sleeves, copper spacers, bushes \u0026 2 LH square cylinder assemblies. Fitted 4 tool holder assemblies, 8 tamping tools and 8 tool-tilting cylinders. Connected greasing hoses and completed greasing. M/c made ready at 18.00 hrs \u0026 trial block attended(18.10-19.00 hrs; SHYP Yd Rd 3, 300 mtrs)",
                         "status":  "FIT",
                         "stepsTaken":  "Waiting HSPL SE \u0026 the material (oil gripping cylinder part code- 23067083) Spoke to the HSPL service manager, has deputed Service Engineer Mr. Sachin to attend the issue. On 14 \u002615.10.2026, Waiting for material \u0026 SE. On 16.10.2026, HSPL SE arrived to the M/c.Checked the material received . On 17.10.2026 HSPL Service Engineer attended all tool-tilting cylinders, 4 nos. of 65 mm pins, and 8 nos. of RH/LH outer tamping tool holders removed. Lubrication sleeves of LH outer front and rear tool holders removed. On 18.10.2026 RH front and rear tool holder lubrication sleeves (04 nos.) and LH front/rear 65 mm pin lubrication sleeves (02 nos.) and RH front 65 mm pin lubrication sleeve (01 no.) removed. RH rear squeezing cylinder fitted. Worn-out portions of all inner tamping tool holders welded. Inner threads of LH front and RH rear tool-holding bolts reconditioned. M/c repair is under Progress. On 19.10.2026, Replaced 4 sets of 65 mm pins, sleeves, copper spacers, bushes \u0026 2 LH square cylinder assemblies. Fitted 4 tool holder assemblies, 8 tamping tools and 8 tool-tilting cylinders. Connected greasing hoses and completed greasing. M/c made ready at 18.00 hrs \u0026 trial block attended(18.10-19.00 hrs; SHYP Yd Rd 3, 300 mtrs)",
