                         "natureOfFailure":  "Category:Mechanical \n M/c under warranty.\n Description of Failure : During daily maintenance of MDU 848 machine it was observed that discharge Conveyor belt got cut in RHS side longitudinally for a length of 3mtrs",
                         "partNo":  "-",
                         "remarks":  "\"During daily maintenance on 10.10.2026, it was observed that the discharge conveyor belt had developed a longitudinal cut of approximately 3 metres on the RHS. The failure occurred while the machine was under warranty.  The damage to the belt may be attributed to excessive friction, misalignment, or contact with a sharp edge or obstruction during conveyor operation. However, the exact cause requires detailed examination by the OEM.  The OEM service engineer (OEPL) was informed, and the damaged belt was attended to. The discharge conveyor belt was completely dismantled on 13.10.2026, and belt pasting work was completed on 14.10.2026. The machine was made ready at 15:30 hrs.  Considering the occurrence of conveyor belt-related failures in WMDU machines, the issue is planned to be discussed in the November 2026 review meeting with the OEM for detailed failure analysis and identification of permanent preventive measures. The discussion will cover all WMDU machines under warranty, namely MDU-837, MDU-845, MDU-848, MDU-849 and MDU-850, to prevent recurrence of similar failures.\"",
